10
00:47:37,142 --> 00:47:43,142
Imagine: John Lennon is a 1988 documentary film directed by
Andrew Solt about English musician John Lennon.

11
00:52:22,857 --> 00:52:28,857
It was released on 7 October 1988, two days before Lennon's 48th
birthday (and nearly eight years after his death).

12
00:57:08,571 --> 00:57:14,571
The film chronicles Lennon's life and musical career as a
member of the Beatles and as a solo artist.

13
01:01:54,285 --> 01:02:00,285
It features recordings that had not been released prior to the film: an acoustic demo of "Real Love" taped in 1979 (an alternate recording of which
would be finished by the Beatles for 1996's Anthology 2) and a rehearsal take of "Imagine" in mid-1971 before the final take was captured.

14
01:06:40,000 --> 01:06:46,000
The film was commissioned by Yoko Ono in 1986.

15
01:11:25,714 --> 01:11:31,714
None of the three former Beatles, Paul McCartney, George Harrison, or Ringo Starr, agreed
to participate in the film, though they reportedly mostly approved of it.

16
01:16:11,428 --> 01:16:17,428
Imagine: John Lennon, with its wealth of archival footage and
narration, received generally positive reviews.

17
01:20:57,142 --> 01:21:03,142
The film's soundtrack was also successful in the United States, reaching No.

18
01:25:42,857 --> 01:25:48,857
31 on the charts and going gold.

19
01:30:28,571 --> 01:30:34,571
Solt and Sam Egan authored a photo book of the same
title as a companion to the film.

20
01:35:14,285 --> 01:35:20,285
The film explores themes of musician, archive footage, rock
singer, mass media, cult of personality.
